Negative control for the frame-reserved column widths (E7).

Takes `headerCell`'s `w-full` off the declared columns that carry no sort
control, so the share is reserved only where a control happens to sit and every
other column is sized from whatever the current page's data measures. That is
E7's defect — the columns resize/jump as a sort swaps the rows under them.

The drop has to be PARTIAL to be a control: `w-full` removed from all of them
leaves the header row uniform, and uniformity across the declared columns is
the whole of what the E7 spec can see (jsdom resolves no widths, so "equal
share" is asserted as one shared treatment, never a measured pixel).

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the actions-anchor spec's E7 block — every declared column gets the same
width treatment, so none is measured from its content.

